      "writtenOn": "2022-05-18T07:34:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I tried to enable google-readability-casting and found more than 20K cases within the first 5% of tidy-soong_subset build. It had also triggered 500+ warnings-as-errors, because some projects just selected too general check list patterns to treat as errors. We will need to fix those before enabling this check by default.\n\nHere is a rough count of cases from enabled google- checks:\n   5063 google-runtime-int\n   3207 google-explicit-constructor\n   2735 google-build-using-namespace\n   2257 google-global-names-in-headers\n   1623 google-default-arguments\n    186 google-upgrade-googletest-case\n     55 google-runtime-operator\n     35 google-build-namespaces\n     24 google-build-explicit-make-pair\n\nWould you like to disable all checks with too many cases?",
      "parentUuid": "53bfb5fd_939e68f9",
      "revId": "93adc4dcf8986d25b41573f26581e9497363ddca",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7fb64575_fede7439",
        "filename": "cc/config/tidy.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 45,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003224
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-05-18T20:30:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "ah, sorry, i hadn\u0027t noticed that `-google-readability*` covered the casting.\n\nyeah, i think _any_ warning that already has thousands of instances is likely to be unworkable... if we make too much noise on every change we\u0027re just going to train people to ignore _all_ errors. (and for the exceptions, they can always opt themselves in.)\n\neven if long-term we end up with a larger set, i think it makes most sense to start small, and \"spend\" our \"being annoying\" budget on the most important stuff --- warnings with *both* a low false-positive rate but also a high likelihood that it\u0027s a _bug_ that really needs to be fixed. (so definitely nothing that\u0027s \"just\" a stylistic opinion.)",
      "parentUuid": "30624ffd_16886a4b",
      "revId": "93adc4dcf8986d25b41573f26581e9497363ddca",
